From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:25:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/30] power: sequencing: qcom-wcn: increase WCN7860 power-up
 delay

WCN7860 shares the WCN7850 power-up sequence and its cold-start
behaviour: when Bluetooth asserts BT_EN while WLAN_EN is still low, the
chip is not ready for the first HCI command 50 ms later, the read of
the QCA version is lost and hci_qca gives up after the 2 s command
timeout ("Reading QCA version information failed (-110)").

Give WCN7860 the 100 ms power-up delay that the previous commit gives
WCN7850. The delay is shared by the Bluetooth and WLAN targets, so a
WLAN power-up also waits 50 ms longer.

Not measured on WCN7860 yet (OnePlus Pad 4): the BT-first cold start is
checked with rfkill cycles while WLAN is down.

Based-on: bd60a639b621 ("power: sequencing: qcom-wcn: increase WCN7850 power-up delay", Shuai Zhang <shuai.zhang@oss.qualcomm.com>)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c b/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c
index 0a70efe86..ab934312c 100644
--- a/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c
+++ b/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-qcom-wcn.c
@@ -444,7 +444,7 @@ static const char *const pwrseq_wcn7860_vregs[] = {
 static const struct pwrseq_qcom_wcn_pdata pwrseq_wcn7860_of_data = {
 	.vregs = pwrseq_wcn7860_vregs,
 	.num_vregs = ARRAY_SIZE(pwrseq_wcn7860_vregs),
-	.pwup_delay_ms = 50,
+	.pwup_delay_ms = 100,
 	.targets = pwrseq_qcom_wcn_targets,
 };
 
